Recipe source: https://github.com/conan-io/conan-center-index/tree/master/recipes/ffmpeg/all
The upstream recipe and its Conan compatibility patches were copied from the
local exported ffmpeg/4.4.4 recipe snapshot. The complete upstream recipe SHA-256
is recorded at the top of conanfile.py. The copied Conan recipe uses the MIT
license in LICENSE. This is not FFmpeg's license.

Local changes: fixed FFmpeg version, disabled unused libfdk_aac/SSL defaults,
and added patches/4.4.4-aiplayer-videotoolbox.patch. The local Conan reference
ffmpeg/4.4.4@aiplayer/vtfix prevents confusion with an unmodified upstream binary.

FFmpeg source: https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-4.4.4.tar.bz2
Source SHA-256 is in conandata.yml. FFmpeg and source-derived patches remain
subject to their upstream licenses; see https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html and
https://ffmpeg.org/doxygen/trunk/md_LICENSE.html . Upstream authorship notices
must be preserved. This directory does not relicense FFmpeg under MIT.
The preserved binutils patch includes its original authorship.

The default recipe still enables GPL components such as libx264. Disabling the
unused nonfree options is not a claim that the resulting application binary
is MIT/LGPL-only or that all binary distribution obligations are fulfilled.
This repository's reproduction workflow prepares a source build, not a signed
or license-audited binary release.
